  "body": "Hole-making tools beyond the twist drill have no kind, and drills get no feeds-and-speeds suggestion.\n\n**Where:**\n- `ToolKind` has `Drill` only: no reamer, spot drill, countersink or combined center drill.\n- `tabulated()` (`crates/app/src/cutting.rs:41`) excludes `Drill`, so CamCraft suggests no feeds for any drill.\n\n**Effect:**\n- A reamer can't be stored with its semantics: no chamfer lead, finish allowance, or slower speed.\n- Spot drills are stored as drills, so their geometry is right but there's no \"spot to a chamfer diameter\" behaviour.\n- No drill gets a starting rpm/feed from the cutting table.\n\n**Fix sketch:**\n- Reamer, spot drill, countersink and center drill kinds, with their op behaviours: ream at a reduced speed with a set allowance; spot or countersink to a stated diameter.\n- Drill rows in the cutting table: feed per rev by diameter and material, as conservative handbook-range values.\n\nEffort: high.\n\n**Done means:** a reamer and a spot drill can be stored and used with their behaviour; drills get a suggested rpm/feed; pinned.\n",
